    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0255" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg171"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr. Beaupré.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 26.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 67 of July 1, last, concerning the Panama Canal. It is receiving
                    consideration.</p>
                <p>There is an error in translation in the twentieth line of the second page of the
                    note inclosed. “Dos compañías” has been translated “two countries” instead of
                    “companies.”</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
